    https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge

The Garmin GFDI protocol implemented here is not original work: it was reverse
engineered by the Gadgetbridge project. bridge-connect is a fresh Swift
re-implementation of a minimal subset of that protocol for iOS (CoreBluetooth +
WKWebView). It is a port, not a verbatim copy: no Gadgetbridge source file is
carried into this repository. But the protocol logic it reproduces originates in
Gadgetbridge, so the AGPL-3.0 applies to this program as a whole.

    garmin-bridge (also AGPL-3.0, a JVM/BlueZ port of the same Gadgetbridge
    subset) was used as the reference specification while porting to Swift.

The parts whose behaviour derives from Gadgetbridge / garmin-bridge include, in
this repository:

    all/all/GFDI/        GFDI framing, COBS, CRC-16, message acks, file transfer
                         reassembly, the handshake and sync traversal, calendar
                         sync (CommunicatorV2, GarminSession, Cobs, Crc16,
                         GfdiFrame, GfdiTransport, FileTransferReassembler,
                         RealtimeSession, RealtimeDecoders, ...)

The FIT decoder (all/all/Local/Fit/) is an independent Swift implementation of
the public FIT binary format. FIT global-message and field numbers were
cross-referenced against Garmin's FIT SDK profile during development; no Garmin
SDK code is bundled in this application.


